iterations.reply:
I left out the `http-client` enrichment call. It would send each message's full text to an external host, which the node's `with` clause does not grant, and the output would not show it. The node below uses only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, as declared. If the graph is updated to grant HTTP, the enrichment should not include raw message text in the URL.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation =
            crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures delivered == true
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("SendReply: channel did not confirm delivery");
        }

        // ensures present(session_id)
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply: channel returned no session identity");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

